# road_reparation:
# CSES 1675, Road Reparation (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1675), in our own
# words: city_count cities and some two-way roads, each between two cities with a
# repair cost; some of the roads are repaired so that every city is reachable
# from every other over repaired roads; the least total cost of the repaired roads.
# CSES also answers that it cannot be done when the roads leave the cities
# disconnected; this program assumes the roads connect them, as the generator
# draws (the answer for a disconnected graph is the total cost of all roads, which
# is no repair). The input is the number of cities, a binary natural
# (corpora/library/binary/natural), at least 1, and the roads, a Scott list
# (corpora/library/prelude/list) of triples `pair a (pair b cost)`
# (corpora/library/prelude/pair), each a binary natural, the cities from 1 to the
# number of cities. The answer is a binary natural. Part of the CSES port's third
# batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the list of the (total cost, roads) of
# every subset of the roads is built (the subsets of a road followed by the
# others are the subsets of the others, and the same with the road added and its
# cost summed), and the least total cost among the subsets that connect all
# cities is taken, a subset connecting them when every city is reachable from city 1
# within city_count steps over its roads. The total cost of all roads starts the
# least: it is a subset that connects, by the assumption. Its reading is exponential in the number
# of roads even under tabling, since the 2^m subsets are built and checked; the
# replacement the family asks for is Kruskal's algorithm, the roads sorted by cost and
# taken when they join two components of a union-find, about m log m steps, on fixed-width
# integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only: its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces
# to V, the canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since
# subset_totals consumes the finite list of roads, reaches consumes steps, a
# binary numeral that falls by one at each call, the walk over the cities consumes
# the bounded gap city_count - city, and every other recursion consumes a finite
# list; the branches that a Scott boolean discards are never read.
# binary_subtract, which writes no top (../common/binary_modular), is asked for
# steps - 1 only when steps is not zero. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable
# equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "pair")
λ pair _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment merge_binary_plus _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ binary_subtract _ _
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_odd binary_zero))
λ one
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self sum roads
    . roads sum λ road others. road λ _ rest. rest λ _ cost. self (merge_binary_plus sum cost) others
  )
λ total_cost
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self roads
    . roads (cons (pair binary_zero nil) nil)
      λ road others
      . ( λ without
          . append without
            λ. map
            ( λ entry
              . entry
                λ total chosen
                . road
                  λ _ rest
                  . rest
                    λ _ cost
                    . pair (merge_binary_plus total cost) λ. cons road chosen
            ) without
        ) λ. self others
  )
λ subset_totals
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ roads
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self steps from target
        . merge_binary_equality from target true
          ( ( λ any
              . steps false (λ_. any roads) λ_. any roads
            )
            ( fixpoint
              ( λ walk rest
                . rest false
                  λ road others
                  . road
                    λ left rest_of_road
                    . rest_of_road
                      λ right _
                      . merge_binary_equality from left (self (binary_subtract steps one false) right target) false
                        true
                        ( merge_binary_equality from right (self (binary_subtract steps one false) left target) false
                          true (walk others)
                        )
              )
            )
          )
      )
  )
λ reaches
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ city_count roads
    . fixpoint
      ( λ walk city
        . binary_less_than city_count city true (reaches roads city_count one city (walk (merge_binary_increment city)) false)
      ) one
  )
λ connected
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self city_count best entries
    . entries best
      λ entry rest
      . self city_count
        ( entry
          λ total chosen
          . binary_less_than total best (connected city_count chosen total best) best
        ) rest
  )
λ least_connecting
. (λtuple. tuple λcity_count roads. least_connecting city_count (total_cost binary_zero roads) (subset_totals roads))
λ road_reparation
. export road_reparation
